// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/widgets/t27c-stages.t27 -- how the t27c compiler works, stage by stage, on the reader's own text
; Source of truth for public/widgets/t27c-stages/ (gHashTag/trinity): scripts/widget-pages-from-spec.mjs
; compiles this file, checks its constants, evaluates the tests below and writes the page; the page
; hands every constant to tool.js as window.T27_WIDGET. tool.js holds no English of its own: every
; word on screen is a SAY_ constant here, every number the tool relies on is a K_ constant.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN). Lesson of the beginner course, gHashTag/trinity#1418.

; WHAT IT DOES: the reader edits a small t27 spec in a text box. After every pause in typing, the
; page hands the text to the real compiler, public/t27/t27_compiler.wasm (t27c built for the browser
; from gHashTag/t27 bindings/wasm-explorer), through its t27_analyze export, in the reader's tab. The
; answer is shown as six stages the reader clicks: the bytes, the tokens the lexer cut, the tree the
; parser built, the type checker's verdict, the HIR (hardware view) and the code each of seven
; backends wrote. When the lexer or the parser threw part of the text away without an error, the
; page says so above the stages, line by line: that is the compiler dropping text silently.

; WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: that the stages are one straight pipe. In t27c each backend reads the
; parser's tree; the type check reports and does not stop them, and only the "Verilog from HIR"
; backend is written from the HIR. The page says this where it shows. It does not claim the type
; checker is complete: a name that was never declared passes it today. A spec with a `use` line
; shows less here than at the command line: the browser has no checkout to resolve imports from.

; DATA PROVENANCE: nothing on the page is precomputed. The K_EXAMPLE_ numbers below (the card's and
; the hook's) are what the same wasm answered in node for SAY_EXAMPLE_SOURCES[0];
; scripts/widget-data/t27c-stages.mjs re-runs it, writes examples.json and fails when they disagree.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

