pub const SAY_STAGE_LINES : [6]str = ["To a compiler your text starts as plain bytes: one number per character, with no meaning yet.", "The lexer cuts the bytes into tokens, the words of the language: a keyword, a name, a number, a bracket. Comments and spaces are left out.", "The parser fits the tokens into a tree that says what holds what: the module holds a function, the function a return, the return an addition.", "The type checker walks the tree and asks whether every value fits the type it was given, such as 300 in a u8, which holds 0 to 255.", "HIR is a hardware view of the module: the wires that come in, the wires that go out and the signals inside.", "Each backend walks the tree and writes the program again in another language: Verilog for chips, C, Rust, Zig, JavaScript and TypeScript."];
